{"kind":"request","text":"Make the repository path the Workroom's primary title and open repository details in an accessible dialog with Branches and Railway tabs, replacing Repository content embedded at the bottom of the Work view.","body":{"branch":"request/ui-repository-dialog","conditions":"The global header no longer says “The Workroom”; it presents the served repository path as the primary, slightly larger title; the repository basename is visually strongest and always remains visible; constrained widths elide the beginning or middle of a long path rather than its basename/end, with regression cases for POSIX roots, one-segment paths, spaces, and very narrow widths; hover and keyboard focus reveal a concise repository summary including the complete path, current branch or detached HEAD, clean/dirty/unavailable state, and configured remotes; activating the path opens a viewport-centered modal Repository dialog; the dialog has an always-visible summary for full path, current checkout status, HEAD, and remotes plus keyboard-operable Branches and Railway tabs; Branches presents all worktree/check-out entries and preserves their current/branch/HEAD/state/association information; Railway reuses the repository history view, truncation warning, selection, and provenance highlighting; the old Repository/Repository context section is removed from the Work view, so repository inspection is available consistently from Work and Activity; the local-only repository projection is extended to return remotes without making repository state durable, and remote URLs never expose embedded usernames, passwords, tokens, or other credentials; local-state loading, partial failure, offline, no-remote, detached, bare, locked, and prunable cases are explicit without explanatory body prose in the main view; opening, switching tabs, and closing change no durable or personal workroom state; the dialog provides an accessible name, focus containment/restoration, Escape and explicit close behavior, internal scrolling, and a responsive full-screen narrow layout; focused service and UI tests cover metadata projection and credential redaction, title hierarchy and truncation, hover/focus summary, dialog/tab behavior, repository-state edge cases, removal from Work, and accessibility; the embedded UI is rebuilt; relevant UI and Go gates pass; an independent agent approves the exact implementation head before merge.","priority":"usability","supersedes_request":"#2745","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}